# Asset and binary files that are ours, and where each came from: `<path or glob> <provenance>`.
# tools/check-game-content.py fails any other; an entry that matches no file fails too.
.github/*.yml our GitHub configuration
.github/*.yaml our GitHub configuration
.github/workflows/*.yml our CI workflows
crates/content-reader-image/src/native/testdata/*.jpg 7x9 and 11x13 pixel images we encoded with the IJG tools for the JPEG decoder tests (#136)
crates/content-reader-layers/src/content/testdata/zipcrypto_*.zip archives we wrote whose members hold made-up bytes, for the encrypted-archive tests (#136)
crates/content-reader-sound/src/fixtures/synthetic-tone.ogg a sine tone we generated for the music reader test (#156)
crates/dashboard-follow/fixtures/series_slot_tag_*.bin our follow protocol's answers over the synthetic recording (#281)
crates/desktop/icons/* the desktop app's icons, drawn for BattlePlan (#9)
crates/recorder-app/icons/* the recorder tray app's icons, drawn for BattlePlan
ui/public/favicon.svg the UI's icon, drawn for BattlePlan (#9)
vendor/eframe/data/icon.png the eframe crate's own icon, vendored with its MIT licence
LICENSE our MIT licence; mods ship the same standard text
crates/engine-dlc/src/dlc_feature_state.rs DLC names the reader matches against the installed DLC files: identifiers, allowed (owner, 26 Nov)
